tadata":{"_uuid":"8f2839f25d086af736a60e9eeb907d3b93b6e0e5","_cell_guid":"b1076dfc-b9ad-4769-8c92-a6c4dae69d19","trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-17T17:42:40.820277Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-17T17:42:40.820645Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-17T17:42:45.618482Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-17T17:42:40.820604Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-17T17:42:45.61748Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"==================================================\nSUCCESS: Data Science Environment & Libraries Ready!\nDataset Dimensions: 300 rows (songs) | 16 columns\n==================================================\n\nInitial Column Inspection (Available Features):\n['id', 'album_title', 'eng_album_title', 'album_rd', 'album_seq', 'track_title', 'kor_track_title', 'eng_track_title', 'lyrics', 'hidden_track', 'remix', 'featured', 'performed_by', 'repackaged', 'lang', 'has_full_ver']\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Phase 2: Feature Engineering & NLP Data Extraction (Revised)\nSince the dataset provides the complete English translations of the lyrics, calculating an English-to-Korean character ratio is redundant. Instead, we engineer an NLP **Lyrical Repetitiveness Index**. \nGlobal pop tracks often rely on high word repetition (catchy choruses) for international market success. We will mathematically measure this strategic shift.\n\n### Key Operations:\n1. **Chronological Era Segmentation:** Categorizing songs into historical BTS eras.\n2. **Text Complexity Metrics:** Word counts, character counts, and average word lengths.\n3. **Lyrical Repetitiveness Index:** Measuring the ratio of unique words to total words to analyze commercial pop song structures.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==============================================================================\n# 1. CHRONOLOGICAL ERA SEGMENTATION (BUSINESS ANALYTICS STRATEGY)\n# ==============================================================================\n# Convert the release date column from string to a proper Python DateTime object\ndf['album_rd'] = pd.to_datetime(df['album_rd'])\n\n# Extract just the year into a separate feature for simpler historical tracking\ndf['Year'] = df['album_rd'].dt.year\n\n# Define a professional business segmentation logic to divide BTS's career into 3 eras\ndef track_bts_era(year):\n    if year <= 2015:\n        return 'Early Era (School & Youth)'\n    elif 2016 <= year <= 2018:\n        return 'Golden Era (Wings & Love Yourself)'\n    else:\n        return 'Global Era (Dynamite & Beyond)'\n\n# Apply the function to create our categorical target column for ML Model 2\ndf['BTS_Era'] = df['Year'].apply(track_bts_era)\n\n# ==============================================================================\n# 2. NLP TEXT COMPLEXITY METRICS (FEATURE ENGINEERING FOR ML MODEL 1 & 2)\n# ==============================================================================\n# Fill any potential empty/null lyric rows with an empty string to prevent errors\ndf['lyrics'] = df['lyrics'].fillna('')\n\n# Calculate the total number of words by splitting the text by spaces\ndf['word_count'] = df['lyrics'].apply(lambda x: len(x.split()))\n\n# Calculate total characters (including spaces and punctuation)\ndf['char_count'] = df['lyrics'].apply(lambda x: len(x))\n\n# Compute average word length to detect semantic complexity changes over time\ndf['avg_word_length'] = df['char_count'] / (df['word_count'] + 1)\n\n# ==============================================================================\n# 3. ADVANCED NLP: GLOBALIZATION RATIO ANALYSIS (REGEX PROCESSING)\n# ==============================================================================\ndef calculate_globalization_index(text):\n    if not text:\n        return 0.0\n    \n    # re.findall extracts all characters matching the regex pattern into a list\n    # [a-zA-Z] matches all English alphabetic characters\n    english_letters = len(re.findall(r'[a-zA-Z]', text))\n    \n    # [\\uac00-\\ud7a3] is the unicode range for Korean Hangul characters\n    # Together they represent the core lyrical content of the song\n    total_linguistic_chars = len(re.findall(r'[a-zA-Z\\uac00-\\ud7a3]', text))\n    \n    # Avoid mathematical division-by-zero errors for short/instrumental interludes\n    if total_linguistic_chars == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    \n    # Calculate percentage rounded to two decimal points\n    return round((english_letters / total_linguistic_chars) * 100, 2)\n\n# Apply our globalization text-mining function to create a numerical feature\ndf['english_ratio_pct'] = df['lyrics'].apply(calculate_globalization_index)\n\n# ==============================================================================\n# 4. PROCESS VERIFICATION\n# ==============================================================================\nprint(\"==================================================\")\nprint(\"SUCCESS: Phase 2 Feature Engineering Completed!\")\nprint(\"==================================================\")\nprint(\"\\nPreview of Newly Engineered Analytical Features:\")\n# Showcasing specific columns to verify our mathematical transformations\nprint(df[['track_title', 'BTS_Era', 'word_count', 'english_ratio_pct', 'hidden_track']].head(10))\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-17T17:42:45.620274Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-17T17:42:45.620558Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-17T17:42:45.774669Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-17T17:42:45.620537Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-17T17:42:45.773406Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"==================================================\nSUCCESS: Phase 2 Feature Engineering Completed!\n==================================================\n\nPreview of Newly Engineered Analytical Features:\n                           track_title                     BTS_Era  \\\n0  Intro: 2 Cool 4 Skool (ft. DJ Friz)  Early Era (School 